    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (76.94) stands as our premier offensive anchor. Facing a beatable arm in Rocker, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** benefits from both a prime #2 slot and a significant situational advantage regarding stolen base upside; the opposing pitcher\u2019s slower delivery speed yields a 2% boost to his already elite sprint-based utility. We are also leaning heavily into the matchup against Cabrera, E. Both **Daulton Varsho** (72.31) and **Tyler Freeman** (69.03) are must-starts, with **Daulton Varsho** benefiting from a favorable xERA of 4.75 and **Tyler Freeman** capitalizing on a substantial +14% park factor boost. These two, alongside **Luis Arraez** (62.02) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (60.03), represent our high-floor core for a day where we are prioritizing volume and stolen base probability.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Drew Gilbert** (47.88), who narrowly missed the cutoff. While **Drew Gilbert** possesses strong platoon utility against Cabrera, E, his assignment to the bottom of the order (-8% adjustment) dragged his efficiency below the thresholds set by **Gavin Sheets** and **Masyn Winn**. We are also closely monitoring **Will Smith** (42.31), whose score is suppressed by a difficult matchup against Detmers. Despite the low score, **Will Smith** remains in the lineup as a stabilizer, though he is the first candidate to be pulled if we find ourselves ahead in the game cap count later tonight. With **Cal Raleigh** and **Lawrence Butler** unavailable, we are banking on the current configuration to maintain our momentum in the SB category.",
